{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You will bring them and plant them.</b> A prayer that they will stand there a long time and not be exiled, like the manner of \"On My holy mountain I planted it\" (Ezekiel 17:23)." "<b>The mountain of.</b> Like \"this good mountain and Lebanon\" (Deuteronomy 3:25), or an allusion to Mount Moriah; therefore it is written after it, \"the foundation of Your dwelling You made, YHWH.\"" "And the meaning of \"You made\" [פעלת]: that You established a sanctuary as a foundation for Yourself, for the place mentioned corresponds to the honored place above, for the places of the earth change corresponding to the star that stands over them. The wise in astrology will understand this." "And the word מִקּדָש is like מִקְדָּש, and like it \"הִשְׁבַתָ מִטֳּהָרוֹ\" (Psalms 89:45), for the dagesh in the tet is added like the dagesh of the qof in מִקְדָּש. And because there was in the qof a moving shva, the dalet was weakened, for there is no practice in all of Scripture [for] a dagesh after a moving shva, apart from the case of שְׁתַּיִם, and I have already mentioned its grammar." "<b>Your hands established.</b> Like \"You made,\" for the meaning is doubled."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {3 "The verse citation 'Psalms 89:45' reflects the Hebrew numbering; this corresponds to Psalms 89:44 in English numbering."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:59.753157012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}